{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1518476-life-and-permanent-modifications","id":1518476,"title":"Life and permanent modifications","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-21T20:01:52-07:00","id":1518476,"title":"Life and permanent modifications","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> M20 How Do You Do That states that mages can get permanent modification including raised attributes by using permanent Life-Sphere Effects. Some questions arise:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can I get rid of Flaws (like Impediment) using this?</li> <li>If the first answer is YES, how many successes? How many experience points needed?</li> <li>If the first answer is YES, can this augmentation be unweaved if you paid XP? If you didnt?</li> <li>Raising attributes costs half experience points, can this augmentation be unweaved if you paid XP?</li> <li>How many successes needed for minor (improved eyesight, hearing, accelerated healing) enhancements? How much XP?</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T08:19:27-07:00","id":1518529,"title":"","content":"Looking at M20 I\u2019d say:<br /> 1. Yes level of Impediment determines sphere level.<br /> 2. These are pretty significant changes (even in mechanical terms) I\u2019d rule it\u2019s between a Mighty or Outlandish Feat so minimum 5 successes, XP would be the cost of buying the impediment off - however high successes could reduce this. (I\u2019d be happy if a Mage has reached Life 3 or 4 they\u2019ve invested some fairly heavy XP already)<br /> 3. Permanent changes require min Life 3/Prime 3 for permanence, if successes and XP are spend no I\u2019d argue it can\u2019t be unwoven without a Mage working the effect in reverse.<br /> 4. As above as the definitions are a little unclear/subjective between between Life 3 (alter self) &amp; Life 4 I\u2019d rule 3 can only permanently increase by up to 3 dots and 4s required for anything above (including stats over 5)<br /> 5. Mighty Feat so up to 5 successes, XP as per Merit cost <br /> <br /> As a house rule I\u2019d rule that Life 4/5 if used for minor effects would lower XP costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}